= Practice Questions (Exam Pattern)

Ten questions designed in authentic CUET UG single-correct style. The official marking scheme awards $+5$ for each correct answer and deducts $-1$ for every incorrect answer.

#mcq(1, [The European Economic Community (EEC) and Euratom were formally established in 1957 by which landmark international treaty?], (
  [Treaty of Versailles], [Treaty of Rome], [Maastricht Treaty], [Treaty of Lisbon],
))

#mcq(2, [In which year did the physical Euro currency notes and coins enter public circulation across participating European Union member states?], (
  [1992], [1999], [2002], [2005],
))

#mcq(3, [Which two European Union member states famously secured opt-out clauses and resisted the adoption of the single European currency (Euro)?], (
  [France and Germany], [Denmark and Sweden], [Italy and Spain], [Poland and Hungary],
))

#mcq(4, [The Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) was founded in August 1967 with the signing of which declaration by five nations?], (
  [Jakarta Declaration], [Manila Declaration], [Bangkok Declaration], [Bandung Declaration],
))

#mcq(5, [Which of the following countries was NOT among the original five founding members of ASEAN in 1967?], (
  [Indonesia], [Thailand], [Vietnam], [Philippines],
))

#mcq(6, [The distinctive diplomatic culture of ASEAN characterized by informal, consensual, and non-confrontational dialogue is popularly referred to as the:], (
  [Asian Century], [ASEAN Way], [Panchsheel Framework], [Look East Doctrine],
))

#mcq(7, [Who announced the historic 'Four Modernisations' (agriculture, industry, defense, and science & technology) in China in 1973?], (
  [Mao Zedong], [Zhou Enlai], [Deng Xiaoping], [Xi Jinping],
))

#mcq(8, [In which year did Deng Xiaoping launch the revolutionary 'Open Door Policy' and economic modernization reforms in China?], (
  [1971], [1976], [1978], [1982],
))

#mcq(9, [In which year did the People's Republic of China formally gain accession to the World Trade Organization (WTO)?], (
  [1978], [1991], [1998], [2001],
))

#mcq(10, [Which Indian Prime Minister made a historic visit to China in December 1988, ending 34 years of diplomatic freeze since the 1962 border war?], (
  [Indira Gandhi], [Rajiv Gandhi], [P.V. Narasimha Rao], [Atal Bihari Vajpayee],
))

= Detailed Solutions

#solution(1, [The Treaty of Rome was signed in March 1957 by France, West Germany, Italy, Belgium, the Netherlands, and Luxembourg, creating the European Economic Community (EEC).], answer: [B])

#solution(2, [While the Euro was introduced electronically in 1999 for banking transactions, physical Euro currency notes and coins entered daily public circulation on 1 January 2002.], answer: [C])

#solution(3, [Denmark and Sweden exercised opt-out provisions from the Maastricht Treaty monetary guidelines, refusing to adopt the Euro and preserving their national currencies.], answer: [B])

#solution(4, [ASEAN was founded on 8 August 1967 with the signing of the Bangkok Declaration by the foreign ministers of Indonesia, Malaysia, Philippines, Singapore, and Thailand.], answer: [C])

#solution(5, [Vietnam was not a founding member in 1967; it was admitted into ASEAN decades later in 1995 following the resolution of the Cambodian conflict.], answer: [C])

#solution(6, [The 'ASEAN Way' is the recognized term for Southeast Asian diplomacy based on quiet informality, non-confrontation, mutual respect for sovereignty, and consensus building.], answer: [B])

#solution(7, [Chinese Premier Zhou Enlai introduced the Four Modernisations in 1973 to upgrade agriculture, industry, national defense, and science & technology.], answer: [B])

#solution(8, [Deng Xiaoping declared the 'Open Door Policy' in December 1978 at the Third Plenum of the 11th Central Committee of the CCP, inaugurating market-oriented reforms.], answer: [C])

#solution(9, [China was officially admitted into the World Trade Organization in December 2001, anchoring its position as the premier manufacturing exporter to the world.], answer: [D])

#solution(10, [Prime Minister Rajiv Gandhi traveled to Beijing in December 1988, holding landmark talks with Deng Xiaoping that normalized diplomatic, trade, and cultural relations.], answer: [B])

